cal for November 13. The normal high for the date is 45\u00b0F, and the record is 65\u00b0F (2016). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Alpena has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Alpena's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Alpena has set <strong class=\"sig\">34 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 89 that chance alone would give, and <strong>104 record highs</strong>, close to the 89 that chance alone would give. The 1950s hold the most record highs of any decade (46). Alpena's all-time high is 106\u00b0F, on July 13, 1936.","t_chg":"Alpena's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 105 complete years: Alpena's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.38), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1918. Alpena's average high shows no clear change: +0.10\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.20) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Alpena's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.07 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 29.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 2017 (40.15 in); the driest, 1925 (17.05 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 2 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}